{"highest":2,"ids":{"red-team lens, medium: When the POST response has no parseable `created_at` (jq falls back to epoch 0, so `_CCGL_RACE_NOTE_AT=0`), the guard is false and `since` stays 0, so every historical concurrent claim note on the issue is included in the read-back; a past epoch's winner note — which is never deleted on release — has the earliest `created_at` and wins, causing the current legitimate run to return `race_lost: true`. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh: \"(( _CCGL_RACE_NOTE_AT > 0 )) && since=$(( _CCGL_RACE_NOTE_AT - 4 * gt ))\"; happens when: A GitHub API POST-comment response without a valid `created_at` field (partial response, proxy truncation, an rc-2 path whose response body lacks the field) while any past winner note exists on the issue — a condition that is permanent after the first successful claim on any issue.; fix: code; ACCEPTED IF: when `_CCGL_RACE_NOTE_AT` is zero the run either refuses with a backend error or uses a `since` value that provably excludes notes from prior label epochs, and a test asserts the correct behavior when the POST reply carries no `created_at`)":"RLREDTEAM-1","red-team lens, medium: If both competing runs post their notes within the same propagation window and each run's read-back executes before the other run's note is visible via the API, both runs see only their own note, both enter this branch, and both return `{\"acquired\": true}`, violating R1 (\"exactly one proceeds\"); none of the DSRACE requirements have a precondition covering this case, and the design's outside assumptions list ordering and stability of `created_at` but do not state that a comment is immediately visible to all API clients after the POST that created it. (plugins/claim-coordinator/github-labels/plugin.sh: \"if [[ -z \"$winner\" || \"$winner\" == \"$my_holder\" ]]; then\"; happens when: Two runs that add the label within milliseconds of each other on GitHub infrastructure where comment reads are served from a replica or cache that has not yet replicated the peer's newly posted note — a narrow but real condition on a busy GitHub host.; fix: design; ACCEPTED IF: the design's outside assumptions explicitly address cross-connection comment visibility consistency, or the design acknowledges the residual window where both runs proceed and states why it is acceptable)":"RLREDTEAM-2"}}
